  "id": "Compound::DB01115 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Nifedipine, a calcium channel blocker, is shown to interact with multiple cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzymes, including Cyp2c8, through a series of mechanistically linked pathways. The evidence suggests that Nifedipine binds to Cyp1a2 and Cyp2c9, both of which are involved in oxidoreductive activities that involve quinone or similar compounds as acceptors. These activities are then linked to Cyp2c8, indicating a potential role in the metabolic processing of substrates. The shared involvement of Cyp2c8 in these pathways implies a possible mechanism by which Nifedipine may influence the activity of this enzyme, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of interaction across different CYP isoforms, suggesting a broader functional relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of CYP2C8 in the metabolism of compounds that undergo oxidative reactions, and Nifedipine's ability to modulate its activity may have implications for drug metabolism and toxicity.",
